{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T21:55:51.449251Z","id":"6dac327567245e1b1da1ff5cfdd6246aae511ea2e85b95e1a98863aa7a276ec0","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:68e766062","references":"aa0d29e9189355d261dcd2299523cc2c65fb2f738375fe200e42553a412df95e","summary":"Re-pointed after the branch was rebased onto main and re-signed: git:d3bb66fd3 is now git:68e766062, with the same subject and change; the rebase met no conflicts.","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:41:42.581707Z","id":"6408cd46ac2d347f3d84d39a91954e40725278aecc9382dbc27dfe4a306936a5","body":{"detail":"The html format (spec §5.2) promises markup without code and with absolute links. A tokenizer pass keeps it linear and needs no new crate (html5ever's tokenizer is already a dependency); html5ever's tree builder would balance the markup but rewrite structure the page wrote. srcset is a list of URL and descriptor pairs and is left as it came. Tests: crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs clean_html_removes_code_and_keeps_structure, relative_links_become_absolute.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1393},"end":{"line":1405},"content_hash":"768ed8eea8ff9542018d6259aa8bce6c9afebee102819bccf3c2038fcb13cb3d"},"summary":"clean_html writes a page back token by token, not as a tree: unbalanced markup stays unbalanced, srcset keeps its relative URLs, and text inside kept raw-text elements (xmp, iframe, noembed, noframes) is escaped as text","tags":["plan:unify-task-8","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:53:51.489240Z","id":"514a70c21cb7eb6f44769ef3c06fc4411024f1664e0e3a14279e74a5f8fdf923","body":{"detail":"Failure: `clax.web.fetch(url, {format: \"html\"})` of a page that opens with `<base href=\"https://x.example/<about 7,900 characters>\">` and then repeats `<b src>` (7 bytes each) to the 5,000,000-byte body cap (`FetchLimits::max_bytes`, crates/clax-bot/src/web/mod.rs:249) makes clean_html build a String of about 714,000 x 8,000 bytes, roughly 5.7 GB. Without a `<base>` the fetched URL alone (up to 2,000 characters, crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs:13) gives about 1.4 GB.\n\nWhy: every attribute named in URL_ATTRS on any element (page.rs:1384-1394), including an empty value, is replaced by `base.join(value)` (page.rs:1475-1480); an empty value joins to the base itself. The `<base href>` accepted as the document base may be MAX_TARGET_BYTES = 8,000 bytes (page.rs:474, 1454). The output starts at `String::with_capacity(html.len())` (page.rs:1555) and is never capped: the 1 MiB page-store cut (STORE_BYTES, page.rs:18) applies only after clean_html returns. The daemon calls it on its fetched body (crates/clax-server/src/web_source.rs CleanHtml arm, after read_capped) and the Worker in read_body (crates/clax-worker/src/web_source.rs, Handling::CleanHtml), where an isolate's 128 MB memory limit is reached by pages of well under 1 MB. The Markdown converter does not have this problem: it stops at STORE_BYTES (crates/clax-bot/src/web/markdown.rs:293). No test of clean_html covers its output size.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1474},"end":{"line":1481},"content_hash":"c8e218d5da2f177abf1d5f72094fd67b4b371ace9dfddb85316bb9446a9993f5"},"suggested_fix":"Bound clean_html's output as html_to_markdown bounds its own: stop writing once `out.len() >= STORE_BYTES` (cut on a character boundary, as the store does). Also cap a joined URL at MAX_URL_CHARS and keep the value as it came when the join is longer. Add a test that a page of repeated `<b src>` under an 8,000-byte `<base href>` comes back at most STORE_BYTES long.","summary":"clean_html writes every URL attribute out as an absolute URL with no output bound, so a small page expands to gigabytes before the page store cuts it to 1 MiB","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:53:51.491780Z","id":"10eb3f0e383e8a99de2321ebb43a272c8f34b2e768e479d7b4c9cc6cd20bb7ce","body":{"detail":"The check is `value.trim_start().to_ascii_lowercase().starts_with(\"javascript:\")` (page.rs:1467-1471), and the value is then passed to `base.join(value.trim())` (page.rs:1477). The WHATWG URL parser, which the url crate implements, removes every ASCII tab and newline from the input and strips leading C0 control characters and spaces before it reads the scheme (https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-basic-url-parser). So `<a href=\"java&#9;script:alert(1)\">` (the tokenizer decodes the character reference) and `<a href=\"&#1;javascript:alert(1)\">` both fail the prefix check and are written out as `href=\"javascript:alert(1)\"`. The function's doc (page.rs:1392-1401) and spec 2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design §5.2 promise that inline code is removed. Also kept as they came: `<iframe srcdoc=\"<script>...</script>\">` (srcdoc is not in URL_ATTRS and is not dropped) and `<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:...\">`. The output is meant as data for the model, but a model that writes it into an artifact or a `clax.browser.open({html})` page gets live script. Record 6408cd46 covers the token-by-token rewrite and srcset, not this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1465},"end":{"line":1481},"content_hash":"6c5b571b8053aeb09a0e7979bc4b7bd189e6c0dc26206a559c45bf130df0aa3a"},"suggested_fix":"Decide on the parsed URL, not the string: after `base.join`, drop the attribute when `u.scheme()` is `javascript` (or anything but http, https, mailto, tel, data for images), and drop it too when the join fails and the raw value, with ASCII tab, newline and leading C0 removed, starts with `javascript:`. Drop `srcdoc` and `http-equiv=refresh` metas. Add tests with `java\\tscript:`, a leading U+0001, and srcdoc.","summary":"clean_html's javascript: filter is a string prefix check before URL parsing, so `java<TAB>script:` and a leading control character pass it and come out as `javascript:` URLs; `srcdoc` keeps its scripts","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:56:24.299589Z","id":"b8499e49a00d1acd11ee0b7ff34abf4117a6048d14f60787a4c778708bc5dd3f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs:1454-1458 accepts a `<base href>` up to MAX_TARGET_BYTES (page.rs:474, MAX_URL_CHARS*4 = 8,000) as doc_base. page.rs:1466-1481: for every attribute in URL_ATTRS (page.rs:1384-1394, `src` among them) whose value is not `#...` and at most MAX_TARGET_BYTES, the value becomes `base.join(value.trim())`; an empty value (`<b src>`) passes both checks and joins to the base without its fragment. The output String (page.rs:1555, capacity html.len()) is pushed to with no length check anywhere in Cleaner::tag or process_token, so 7 input bytes become about `<b src=\"<base>\">`, roughly 8,000 bytes. The input reaches 5,000,000 bytes (FetchLimits::default, crates/clax-bot/src/web/mod.rs:246-252); callers: crates/clax-server/src/web_source.rs:558 read_capped then :587-590 clean_html(&html, &at), and crates/clax-worker/src/web_source.rs:633-635. `git show main:crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs | grep -n 'fn clean_html'` prints nothing, so the function is new on this branch and the failure reaches users only after merge: a blocker.","kind":"comment","references":"514a70c21cb7eb6f44769ef3c06fc4411024f1664e0e3a14279e74a5f8fdf923","summary":"confirmed: an empty URL attribute joins to the document base, and clean_html's output has no bound","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:56:24.300997Z","id":"297ae67a07564229ff9fc3d8d30a412673948e44486bcfa98ee2083cb8bf4254","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs:1467-1473 skips an attribute only when `value.trim_start().to_ascii_lowercase().starts_with(\"javascript:\")`; Rust's trim_start removes Unicode White_Space, not U+0001, and a tab inside the scheme is untouched. page.rs:1474-1480 then writes `base.join(value.trim())`, and the WHATWG basic URL parser (https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-basic-url-parser) removes ASCII tab/newline anywhere and leading C0-control-or-space, so `java\\tscript:alert(1)` and `\\u{1}javascript:alert(1)` parse as scheme `javascript` and are written out as `javascript:alert(1)`. `srcdoc` is not in URL_ATTRS (page.rs:1384-1394), is not an `on...` attribute (page.rs:1463), and is written back with only `&` and `\"` escaped (page.rs:1418-1426), so its markup, scripts included, survives. The doc comment at page.rs:1396-1401 promises `javascript:` URLs removed. Kind concern is right: the output is data for the model, so harm needs a further step.","kind":"comment","references":"10eb3f0e383e8a99de2321ebb43a272c8f34b2e768e479d7b4c9cc6cd20bb7ce","summary":"confirmed: the javascript: check is a string prefix test on the raw value, while the join strips tabs and leading C0 controls","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T16:39:12.847451Z","id":"3352cc87770a0e67247832aecbb0f2654c5b748fec440dfc47cf4e24e73eba9a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:72b265c78fe2","summary":"Fixed in 72b265c78: clean_html writes nothing past STORE_BYTES and keeps a joined URL only within MAX_URL_CHARS; the test failed at 5,600,000 bytes before the fix. Evidence: web::page::tests::clean_html_output_is_bounded, which failed on the code before the fix, passes in //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test; `PATH=~/.local/homebrew/bin:$PATH just check` at 45cd24c07 printed 'Executed 85 out of 407 tests: 407 tests pass.' and 'bazel: all checks passed'","supersedes":"514a70c21cb7eb6f44769ef3c06fc4411024f1664e0e3a14279e74a5f8fdf923","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T16:39:13.071307Z","id":"d982bbc44db6ae2c0729d08131fad44b2be8fd40ae3a1dabddff207708a00aea","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:47208f993f7d","summary":"Fixed in 47208f993: javascript: is read as the URL parser reads it (tabs, newlines and leading C0 skipped, and the joined URL's scheme), srcdoc and meta refresh are dropped; before the fix java&#9;script: came out as href=\"javascript:alert(1)\". Only javascript: is filtered: an allowlist of schemes is not built. Evidence: web::page::tests::clean_html_drops_hidden_script, which failed on the code before the fix, passes in //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test; `PATH=~/.local/homebrew/bin:$PATH just check` at 45cd24c07 printed 'Executed 85 out of 407 tests: 407 tests pass.' and 'bazel: all checks passed'","supersedes":"10eb3f0e383e8a99de2321ebb43a272c8f34b2e768e479d7b4c9cc6cd20bb7ce","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
